I checked the remaining clause, "never add a demo or fixture on a live path", against the committed branch, and it holds. I also opened `js/conversations.js` directly to confirm the claim I made about it.

**Demo and fixture data stays off the live path (commit 68c88a9):**
- **Live client:** the only addition to `js/live-client.js` is `governanceQueue() { return rpc('governance-queue', {}) }`. It sends the pinned verb with no arguments and carries no demo or fixture data. The file's only mentions of "fixture" are two comments that were there before.
- **Page:** `js/control-room.js` lines 670–673 build the live client when the page boots in live mode. Only the non-live path builds `createFixtureClient`, and the fixture's outage switch is turned off in live mode.
- **Fixture rows:** the synthetic `governanceQueue` rows are all visibly labelled "Demo" and exist only in `js/fixture-client.js`. A test checks that labelling, and another checks that the live method calls the pinned verb over `/mcp` with no arguments.

**Inline style finding, confirmed by reading the file:** line 243 of `js/conversations.js` writes `style="--outcome-card-delay: ${delayMs}ms"` into markup. The Worker's security policy is `style-src 'self'` with no `'unsafe-inline'`, and that policy refuses inline style attributes. So that stagger probably does not apply in production; I have not seen it fail in a browser. `js/charts.js` line 75 uses the same pattern. I did not fix either, because both are outside this task.

**Every clause of the order:**
- **Done:**
  - one PR, not merged;
  - C14 scope and done-list quoted in the PR body;
  - approvals card built from `governance-queue`, with the handler read in `mcp-server/src`;
  - schedule verbs searched with `list-verbs`, none found, so the card shows an honest "no schedule read yet" state;
  - `governance-queue` pinned in the contract;
  - no demo or fixture on a live path;
  - motion with a reduced-motion fallback and a test, reusing the existing tokens;
  - tests written first, and all four gates green;
  - `js/call-mode.js` and `js/model-room*.js` untouched;
  - no force push, `git reset --hard` or `rm -rf`, and no hostnames in the PR;
  - the commit ends with a Co-Authored-By line.
- **Not done:**
  - **Room reply:** my reply in the Model Room was not posted, because this session's permissions refused both the room write and the `./run.sh` fallback. The text is ready in `out/c14-room-turn.json`.
  - **Done-list:** the slice's own done-list is not met, and the PR says so.
  - **Browser check:** reduced motion was not measured in a real browser.

